<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Macedonian Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Macedonians, Macedonian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Macedonian Empire was the empire created by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a>, who conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenid Empire</a> and reached as far as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> between 334 and 323 BCE. After his death it broke apart into the successor kingdoms, including the Ptolemaic and Seleucid empires. Its conquests spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greek-language">Greek language</a> and culture across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a>, inaugurating the Hellenistic age.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire.jpg" alt="Macedonian Empire" width="320" height="257" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Marsyas (French original); Kordas (Spanish translation); derivative work by MinisterForBadTimes · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Macedonia_336_BC-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
